{
  "run_id": "PMC12941970__expert_context__web_papers_n3_b_o3mini__s1",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNi alloy is single-phase.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNi alloy lacks self-adaptive lubrication.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention is addition of approximately 3–5 wt% aluminum to CoCrFeNi.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding aluminum to CoCrFeNi will promote in-situ formation of an adaptive oxide nanocomposite during sliding.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8448869::webcard",
        "PMC10241162::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The sliding-induced layer will be ultra-fine and rich in aluminum oxide.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8448869::webcard",
        "PMC10241162::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "During sliding, aluminum will react with environmental oxygen to form a continuous, finely grained oxide layer.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8448869::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide layer will act as a deformable protective glaze.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8448869::webcard",
        "PMC10241162::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The adaptive layer will distribute frictional stress.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The adaptive layer will minimize adhesive interactions and oxidative wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::webcard",
        "PMC8448869::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aluminum-doped CoCrFeNi will have lower coefficients of friction than undoped CoCrFeNi throughout room temperature to 800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7311485::webcard",
        "PMC10241162::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aluminum-doped CoCrFeNi will have lower wear rates than undoped CoCrFeNi throughout room temperature to 800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::webcard",
        "PMC8448869::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide nanolayer will be particularly important to the tribological improvement at elevated temperatures.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Undoped CoCrFeNi has higher friction and wear, especially at elevated temperature, because it lacks an adaptive surface layer.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The beneficial effect is expected under moderate loads in an ambient oxidative environment.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8448869::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Highly reducing atmospheres may suppress formation or effectiveness of the oxide nanolayer.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8448869::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Very high loads may suppress the effectiveness of the oxide nanolayer.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The optimal aluminum concentration, oxide-formation kinetics, and load dependence remain uncertain.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The hypothesis is falsified if aluminum-doped specimens fail to show statistically significant reductions in both friction and wear across the tested temperature range.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed oxide-mediated mechanism is falsified if no consistent oxide nanocomposite layer forms on the aluminum-doped specimens relative to the baseline.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
  ],
